WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:04.910
Even during this age in which a new great
TV show seems to premiere every couple of

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:07.280
weeks, there are a few clear standouts.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:10.840
These all deserve to be included in the best
TV seasons of all time.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:16.620
Breaking Bad is one of those shows that is
about as perfect as television gets.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:21.019
That said, the further along the show progresses,
the more tense and action-packed it becomes.

00:00:21.019 --> 00:00:24.820
Choosing between seasons four and five is
tough, but we have to give the nod to the

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:27.120
absolutely riveting final season of the show.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:31.240
When season five starts, Walter White has
ascended to the top of the drug trade.

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:35.120
He's eliminated his greatest rival and seemingly
nothing stands in his way.

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:39.200
However, such an astronomical high paves the
way for a devastating fall.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:43.370
The season pays off everything the story has
been setting up - and throws in a few killer

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:47.890
twists along the way, including the moment
Walt's brother-in-law Hank discovers Walt

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:51.240
is the mysterious meth kingpin that he's been
chasing for years.

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:54.140
["I gotta say, I don't like the way you're
looking at me right now."

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:06.140
It all blows up in the final three episodes,
one of which, "Ozymandias," is a serious contender

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:08.500
for the best episode of television ever made.

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:12.380
There are few TV series more divisive than
Lost.

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:16.700
Still, despite the controversy, the show's
first season is a genuinely special piece

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:17.380
of television.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:21.320
Right from the pilot, the season hooks you
in with stellar character work and plenty

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:22.580
of engaging mysteries.

00:01:22.829 --> 00:01:26.980
It builds its characters with stunning efficiency
and economy, perfectly balancing character

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:29.880
histories with exploration of the island's
mysteries.

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:34.180
Later seasons would skew this balance too
far in either direction, but the show's debut

00:01:34.189 --> 00:01:38.680
season gives as much attention to the mystery
of the hatch as it does to Jack's relationship

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:39.920
with his departed father.

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:44.880
From the perfect pilot to the riveting finale,
season one of Lost is just as good today as

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:46.100
it was when it first aired.

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:53.380
"I've looked into the eye of this island,
and what I saw was beautiful."

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:59.600
Parks and Recreation really hit its stride
around its third season, but season four cemented

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:02.080
the show as an all-time great television comedy.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:10.580
[Laughter]

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:15.240
Even without the season-long throughline of
Leslie's city council campaign, season four

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:20.270
provides several all-time great episodes,
including "Ron and Tammys" and "Pawnee Rangers."

00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:25.100
Paul Rudd's Bobby Newport absolutely steals
the entire season as he wanders in and out

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:28.280
of the season with a guilelessness that few
other actors could pull off.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:31.180
"We're not gonna quit the campaign.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:33.020
Why would we do that?"

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:33.820
"Because!

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:35.980
I want it.”

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:40.860
It's the most memorable, most quotable season
of an already very memorable and quotable

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:41.360
comedy.

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:43.440
"You get fired, I'll quit and we'll leave
together.

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:44.640
I'm serious.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:50.520
Move to a new city, change our names, burn
our fingertips off with acid, swap faces."

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:51.120
“What?”

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:55.620
We live in an era in which superhero shows
and movies are a dime a dozen.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:03:00.680
The best way for one to stand out is to center
itself around unique themes, and Jessica Jones'

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:03.760
first season does this better than just about
any entry in the genre.

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:09.030
The season serves as a 13-episode meditation
on trauma, abuse, and recovering from toxic

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:10.030
relationships.

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:14.050
It never flinches from the unpleasantries
of such subject matter, and handles it with

00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:15.480
the delicate touch necessary.

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:19.820
Past that, it's anchored by a very strong
hero and a very strong villain.

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:24.540
Krysten Ritter shines as Jessica, while David
Tennant turns out a uniquely menacing performance

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:25.920
as the villainous Kilgrave.

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:30.600
Shocking and emotionally resonant, these episodes
will leave audiences reeling for years.

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:36.240
Justified is anchored by the compelling rivalry
between Timothy Olyphant's U.S. Marshal Raylan

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:40.300
Givens and the magnetic criminal Boyd Crowder,
played by Walton Goggins.

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:41.480
"What're you packing?"

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:44.420
"You'll pay to find that out."

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:48.840
"Oooh, you got ice-cold water running through
your veins."

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:53.700
However, as stellar as the interplay between
those two is, it's not the focus of the series'

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:54.560
best season.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:58.400
That honor goes to the second season's story
revolving around the Bennett family.

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:02.980
The Bennetts run a crime enterprise dealing
in everything from moonshine to marijuana.

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:07.010
Raylan is charged with bringing them down
and as you might expect, things don't go according

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:07.540
to plan.

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:11.840
The way the season establishes the series'
setting of Harlan, Kentucky as the kind of

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:15.980
hometown you can never fully escape makes
for a pitch perfect story and a great piece

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:17.600
of development for Raylan himself.

00:04:17.989 --> 00:04:22.160
Of particular note is Margo Martindale doing
what is easily the best work of her career

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:25.100
as Mags, a terrifying rattlesnake of a crime
boss.

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:26.600
"Coover, I know you're sorry.

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:32.360
That's why it's gonna hurt so much to have
to do this."

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:40.100
Bloodline revolves around the Rayburns, a
large family residing in the Florida Keys.

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:43.931
When their oldest son Danny returns from an
extended disappearance, events are set in

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:46.980
motion that lead to Danny's death at the hand
of his brother John.

00:04:47.110 --> 00:04:50.420
The show chronicles the march to Danny's murder
nonlinearly.

00:04:50.439 --> 00:04:54.800
Rather than obsessing about the plot, most
of Bloodline is carried through conversations,

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:57.500
micro-aggressions, and slowly simmering feuds.

00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:01.639
Bloodline's first season is an addictive,
compelling family drama that will leave you

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:04.840
screaming at your TV by the finale's closing
moments.

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:10.440
Season four of New Girl sees the show regain
its footing after an uneven third season and

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:12.820
truly become the best possible version of
itself.

00:05:13.270 --> 00:05:18.420
More than any season of New Girl, these episodes
delve into hilariously exploring modern dating,

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:21.420
like when Jess downloads a pseudo-Tinder app
for the first time.

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:25.710
That said, the easy standout is "Background
Check," which ranks among the greatest TV

00:05:25.710 --> 00:05:26.920
episodes of all time.

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:31.580
The story sees the gang subject to an in-home
background check as part of Winston's application

00:05:31.599 --> 00:05:32.789
to become a police officer.

00:05:32.789 --> 00:05:36.240
Over the course of the examination, the crew
spirals into insanity.

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:41.060
"I just need you to pretend like you're in
a relationship with this grown man that I

00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:41.560
know - Ah!

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:44.100
I did not think this through.

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:44.940
I did not think this through."

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:49.420
Easily one of the odder sitcoms in recent
memory, New Girl was never more irreverent

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:51.580
or wonderful than it was during its fourth
season.

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:57.100
By the time the sixth season of Game of Thrones
comes around, the story has progressed past

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:59.600
territory covered by the book series it's
drawn from.

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:03.900
This left the showrunners free to run wild
with the story and take it in new, surprising

00:06:03.909 --> 00:06:06.240
directions that can't be spoiled by the books.

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:10.320
They build a number of conflicts to a head,
like the war between the Starks and Boltons

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:14.480
for control of the north, and pepper in a
hefty number of game-changing revelations.

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:28.680
From Daenerys finally making her way to Westeros
to the Battle of the Bastards, Game of Thrones'

00:06:28.689 --> 00:06:30.809
sixth season is riveting genre television.

00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:36.779
In just eight episodes, True Detective's first
season accomplished more in terms of creativity

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:40.180
and critical acclaim than some shows do in
ten-season runs.

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:44.650
The miniseries stars Woody Harrelson and Matthew
McConaughey as surly detectives attempting

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:46.140
to solve a series of murders.

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:51.460
The story is told nonlinearly and features
some seriously dark philosophical tangents,

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:54.320
which creates even more mysteries for the
viewer to solve.

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:56.160
"You get any sleep last night?”

00:06:57.460 --> 00:06:58.400
“I don't sleep.

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:00.620
I just dream.”

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:06.080
True Detective wears its influences on its
sleeve from the start.

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:10.659
It's packed with Lovecraftian themes and structure,
making a story about two men hunting a killer

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:11.820
feel otherworldly.

00:07:11.940 --> 00:07:16.580
It borrows from plenty of well-loved literature,
but the show doesn't simply rip off these

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:17.080
stories.

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:21.620
Instead, it uses them to create a depth of
influence, to give viewers more to dissect.

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:30.800
"I contemplate the moment in the garden, the
idea of allowing your own crucifixion."

00:07:30.969 --> 00:07:35.460
When this is combined with the dense themes,
fully formed characters, and complex plot,

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:39.439
the result is a show you can analyze and break
down a million different ways.

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:43.380
It's massively compelling television, the
likes of which we haven't seen since.

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:49.340
Much of the first season of A.I. sci-fi drama
Westworld centers on the idea of a maze.

00:07:49.340 --> 00:07:54.029
The show's characters, both human and robot,
find themselves drawn into a conspiracy involving

00:07:54.029 --> 00:07:57.140
a maze symbol left by one of Westworld's original
founders.

00:07:57.260 --> 00:08:01.539
While it's easy to get distracted by the stellar
performances and special effects, the mystery

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:03.720
is what makes the show so memorable and addictive.

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:08.300
"I think there's a deeper meaning hiding under
all that.

00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:13.140
Something the person who created it wanted
to express."

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:18.060
Modern TV shows love mysteries, but few shows
manage to pay them off in ways that don't

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:19.580
cheat the viewer in some way.

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:22.880
Westworld is the rare mystery that never makes
this mistake.

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:25.960
Its plot is structured like the maze it revolves
around.

00:08:25.969 --> 00:08:30.680
By the time we reach the center of the maze,
it's just as shocking to us as it is to them.

00:08:30.680 --> 00:08:33.139
It's an amazing start to an amazing series.

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:36.949
Few shows have changed the game like The Sopranos.

00:08:36.949 --> 00:08:40.959
The modern concept of prestige television
can be traced back to the runaway success

00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:42.520
of HBO's mob drama.

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:46.470
The whole run is excellent, right up to the
finale, and the acclaim and awards speak for

00:08:46.470 --> 00:08:46.980
themselves.

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:51.400
Look no further than the show's immaculate
second season as evidence as to why it still

00:08:51.410 --> 00:08:53.459
holds the reputation it enjoys today.

00:08:53.459 --> 00:08:57.640
It used to be far more outside the norm for
shows to kill major characters with little

00:08:57.640 --> 00:08:58.500
to no warning.

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:03.740
The Sopranos made its bones in this trade,
and focuses its sophomore season on Tony Soprano's

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:06.100
best friend becoming an FBI informant.

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:10.910
The story spirals to an inevitable confrontation
between the two that plays out just as shockingly

00:09:10.910 --> 00:09:12.600
today as it did when it first aired.

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:17.460
Even with all the stellar prestige TV shows
on the air today, we can't forget the original.

00:09:18.980 --> 00:09:22.520
There's very little to say about The Wire
that hasn't already been said.

00:09:22.520 --> 00:09:25.600
It's perhaps the single most acclaimed television
show of all time.

00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:30.730
The Wire's tale of the complex lives of Baltimore
cops and criminals form a tremendously powerful

00:09:30.730 --> 00:09:35.620
narrative about life, death, poverty, corruption,
and finding the light amidst it all.

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:40.440
While every batch of episodes has its strengths,
season four of The Wire is easily the best

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:44.089
the show has to offer - and when you're talking
about the best season of possibly the best

00:09:44.089 --> 00:09:46.690
show of all time, you know it's something
special.

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:50.769
The show's fourth season sees the narrative
weave a story about the Baltimore school system

00:09:50.769 --> 00:09:53.920
and follows the lives of four young boys who
have grown up in the area.

00:09:54.209 --> 00:09:58.220
While there are other stories going on throughout
the season, the four boys become the season's

00:09:58.220 --> 00:09:58.720
linchpin.

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:03.540
Season four is where the show stops asking
questions and starts giving answers, boldly

00:10:03.550 --> 00:10:08.279
claiming that in a world ravaged by systemic
poverty, there is no level playing field for

00:10:08.280 --> 00:10:09.420
those who grow up in it.

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:12.700
Their fate is predetermined and impossible
to escape.

00:10:12.700 --> 00:10:15.160
As street dealer Bodie tells hard-nosed cop
McNulty:

00:10:16.540 --> 00:10:17.640
"This game is rigged, man.

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:21.220
We're like the little bitches on the chessboard."

00:10:22.440 --> 00:10:22.940
"Pawns."

